  "slug": "systemin-acid-triggers-270d",
  "summary": "New work links peptide and pathogen elicitors to receptor sensitivity, NLR-dependent cell death, and SAR across crop and model plants.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is how plants perceive diverse elicitors and convert them into immune outputs. A Nicotiana systemin study reports four new bioactive systemins detected by SlSYR1 and a premature stop codon in SYR1 orthologs of LAB N. benthamiana, explaining lineage-specific insensitivity. UvWSC1 from Ustilaginoidea virens triggers OsCPK13- and SOBIR1-dependent cell death, while SCMV HC-Pro triggers ADR1/NRG1-dependent hypersensitive death modulated by P3N-PIPO. N-hydroxypipecolic acid is reported to trigger SAR against wheat leaf rust. Arabidopsis UGT74F1 and UGT74F2 restrict turnip mosaic virus independently of salicylic acid, jasmonate and RNA silencing. A mild SCMV vector for maize is a methodological addition rather than part of this immunity thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
